# The gtag snippet in index.html, about.html and privacy.html is allowed by a
# SHA-256 hash in the Content-Security-Policy. That hash is computed over the
# exact bytes of the script body, which are LF while the rest of those files
# are CRLF.
#
# Git's default autocrlf would rewrite those LFs to CRLF on checkout, changing
# the hash and silently blocking the tag — the page would look fine and
# Analytics would record nothing. Deploys currently upload the working tree so
# this has not bitten, but it would the moment anyone clones the repo or
# Vercel's Git integration builds from a checkout.
#
# -text disables all end-of-line conversion for these files: git stores and
# restores them byte for byte.
*.html -text
